{
  "configuration_id": "config_024",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) at 0.619 acc. The image modality contributed ~4 pts over RNA-only in singleprofile (0.485→0.527) yet was very weak alone (0.208), suggesting the ResNet50 encoder may not be extracting sufficient cellular morphology features. Question tested: Does upgrading the image encoder from ResNet50 to ImageNet-pretrained ViT-L unlock more complementary visual information in the multiprofile+avgpool+concat setup? Why this is the best next experiment: It isolates a single high-impact variable (image encoder quality) while holding all other parameters at their known-best values (multiprofile, avgpool, concat, pca_n2000), making the result cleanly interpretable. If ViT-L improves performance, it opens a productive direction; if not, we learn the image contribution is encoder-limited and should focus budget on RNA encoder alternatives (scvi/scgpt). This is more informative than testing fusion type (concat vs weighted showed negligible difference) or transformer aggregation (already shown inferior to avgpool)."
}

